title: "MCP Graph Workflow: Execution Graph for PRD-Driven Development"
abstract: >-
  MCP Graph Workflow is a local-first execution graph built on the Model
  Context Protocol (MCP). It converts product requirement documents (PRDs)
  into persistent task graphs stored in SQLite, integrates a retrieval-
  augmented generation (RAG) pipeline, and orchestrates multi-agent
  development workflows with deterministic phase gates, a composite
  Harnessability Score, and a task-level Model Router. The system is the
  subject of ongoing Master's research in Computer Engineering.
type: software
